","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/0","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/1","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2","document:line:25","/body/constraints","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/7","/body/constraints/8","/body/stories","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/4","/citations/0","/citations/7","/citations/8","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-206db3426ffd4428.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-def.json","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/DEF.md","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md","AGENTS.md",".insrc/artifacts/EPIC-206db3426ffd4428.json",".insrc/artifacts/EPIC-6d6cfaf9a9b14bd4.json",".insrc/artifacts/STORY-6d6cfaf9a9b14bd4-s1.json",".insrc/artifacts/STORY-6d6cfaf9a9b14bd4-s2.json",".insrc/artifacts/STORY-6d6cfaf9a9b14bd4-s3.json","src/daemon/__tests__/workflow-progress-map.test.ts:16-66","src/daemon/__tests__/analyze-progress.test.ts:107-180","src/mcp/__tests__/progress-forward.test.ts:20-72","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress.ts"],"limitations":["The source conversation cited by /citations/8 is unavailable in the supplied context and inspected local records. Its citation states only 'consolidate all long-running progress stories into one epic.' Consequently, stakeholder intent concerning the exact retirement inventory, source-story preservation and approval/link-before-retirement ordering could not be independently verified. The DEF itself explicitly requires approved successor linkage before retirement."],"advice":["Before retiring tracker entries, record a concrete crosswalk from the July issue #41 and stories S001–S003 to the successor epic and stories, including completed capabilities retained and requirements superseded. The successor EPIC artifact already records tracker binding #146.","For this DEF scope assessment, prose adequately explains the required ownership and user-visible behavior. No authored visual definitions, generated companions or renderings are attached; no visual verification is claimed. Detailed interaction and UX artifacts can be assessed when the corresponding designs exist."]},{"chunkId":"contract","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector and its cited evidence. Producer assumptions are supported, and the shared contract covers measured progress, attempt isolation, authorization, bounded reconnects and cancellation separation. One upstream restart-recovery requirement lacks explicit acceptance coverage.","findings":[{"id":"contract-restart-recovery","severity":"MED","location":"docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:72","message":"The shared foundation specifies reconnect snapshots and unavailable-owner handling, but never requires recovery across a daemon restart. The cited SPEC explicitly requires durable snapshots/milestones, preserved terminal outcomes, and interrupted/unknown execution until the owner verifies survival or genuine resumption. Reconnecting to an unchanged daemon can satisfy the current acceptance criteria without exercising this boundary; marking missing progress stale also does not establish an honest execution state. Add a restart acceptance scenario covering retained state, owner revalidation and delayed prior-execution events, without restarting work.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:55","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:72","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:73","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md:33 — R10","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md — acceptance scenarios A8 and A13","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md — Non-functional targets: existing progress is transient and not persisted"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/assumptions","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/body/constraints/6","/body/stories/0","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/4","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/6","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-206db3426ffd4428.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-def.json","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md","src/daemon/__tests__/workflow-progress-map.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/analyze-progress.test.ts","src/mcp/__tests__/progress-forward.test.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress-persistence.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts:112","src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:475","src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts:703","src/mcp/progress-forward.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["When designing adapters, distinguish producer sequence counters from meaningful-progress revisions: existing review heartbeats and repeated analyze stage events advance their sequence/index without necessarily measuring new work.","No visual definitions or generated companions are attached to this DEF. Its shared-contract requirements can be assessed from prose; no visual rendering verification is claimed."]},{"chunkId":"producers","status":"passed","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the cited upstream requirements and current producer evidence. The producer stories preserve existing results, frames and cancellation; distinguish available workflow token batches from analysis stage-only progress; cover review retries, follow-up work and attempt authority; and address nested test results, reporter failure, abort and exit semantics. Their dependencies on the shared foundation are feasible. No demonstrated blocking defect was found within this assignment.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/2","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/3","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/body/constraints/6","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/6","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-206db3426ffd4428.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-def.json","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/DEF.md","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md — R2, R3, R8–R12, R17 and A2, A3, A8, A9, A16, A17","src/daemon/__tests__/workflow-progress-map.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/analyze-progress.test.ts","src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:466","src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts:550","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts — workflow.run and analyze.run.start registrations","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts:113","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/progress.test.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/progress.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/coordinator.ts — attempt recovery, progress observation and publication boundaries","src/workflow/review/design-review/__tests__/coverage-progress.test.ts","src/daemon/tools/builtins/test/index.ts:212","src/daemon/tools/builtins/test/__tests__/test-runner-parity.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["In downstream designs, enumerate the supported workflow/analyze entry points and managed test reporters in an acceptance matrix. Include legacy terminal frames, observer absence, cancellation, unknown measurements, and explicit pass/fail/skip and elapsed-time assertions.","The assigned producer requirements are adequately assessable from prose at DEF stage. No visual definitions or generated companions are attached, and no visual rendering verification is claimed."]},{"chunkId":"vscode","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The assigned sections cover inline routing, attempt isolation, reconnects, runtime-owned retention and aggregate completion. Conversation closure/removal loses an explicit upstream lifecycle requirement.","findings":[{"id":"vscode-conversation-closure","severity":"MED","location":"docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md §6.5, acceptance criteria ac1–ac3","message":"The VS Code story defines chat switching, reconnecting and lost ownership, but does not define what happens to running tasks when their owning conversation is explicitly closed or removed. The cited SPEC R15 explicitly requires a detach/cancel disposition for this boundary. Neither stopping observation nor losing an owner determines that disposition. Add a requirement and acceptance scenario specifying whether execution continues, how retention associations are released, and where surviving results remain accessible; cancellation must retain the existing explicit-request and verified-termination semantics.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md §6.5 ac1–ac3","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md §5 k6–k7","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md — R15: explicit conversation closure/removal disposition","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md — R8: stopping observation versus cancellation","src/daemon/chat-sessions.ts — drop(), close() and dispose()"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/4","/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/constraints/3","/body/constraints/5","/body/constraints/6","/body/constraints/7","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/1","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/7","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-206db3426ffd4428.json","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md","AGENTS.md","vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-file-store.ts — evictBeyondCap","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts — status projection, detached observation and terminal paths","vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts — lifecycle and lease seams","src/daemon/chat-sessions.ts",".insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-def.json — completed substantive feedback"],"limitations":[],"advice":["At downstream design, explicitly map extension conversation, daemon session, native session, invocation, task and attempt identities. Current protocol targeting and daemon pool identifiers are distinct.","Include Stop, setup failure, process death and detached-observer reconciliation in lifecycle validation. Current code contains separate status-writing paths that must share task-aware projection.","No UX definitions or generated companions are attached to this DEF; no visual rendering was verified. The prose supports DEF-stage assessment. Downstream UX artifacts should demonstrate concurrent task messages, terminal compaction and reconnect restoration."]},{"chunkId":"cli","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector and linked evidence. Token gating, original results, fixed fallback cadence, duplicate suppression and degraded recovery are covered. Native background lifetime qualification and user-visible fallback cost disclosure lose explicit upstream requirements.","findings":[{"id":"cli-background-lifetime","severity":"MED","location":"docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:151","message":"Native qualification lists connectivity, token forwarding, visible rendering and scheduling, but omits background/session lifetime as a separate capability. The cited SPEC requires this distinction and explicit reporting when vendor session activity cannot be maintained. Passing an in-request rendering test and a scheduling test does not establish observation after the launching turn ends or the native session exits. Add acceptance coverage for these boundaries per supported client/version/session, including honest limitation reporting and retained task/results for later reattachment without extending an expired progress token.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:150","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:151","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:153","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md — R5, R7, R16; A4, A6, A15"]},{"id":"cli-fallback-cost-disclosure","severity":"LOW","location":"docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:152","message":"The fallback is described internally as token-consuming and requires opt-in, but no requirement makes its token consumption and ordinary chat messages visible to the user. The upstream SPEC explicitly requires that disclosure. Preserve it in the opt-in acceptance scenario, including that unchanged polls can still consume tokens.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md — k5 and s6 ac3","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md — R6; A5, A10"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/5","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/constraints/3","/body/constraints/4","/body/constraints/6","/body/constraints/7","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2","/citations/2","/citations/5","/citations/7","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-206db3426ffd4428.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-def.json — completed substantive feedback","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md","src/mcp/__tests__/progress-forward.test.ts","src/mcp/progress-forward.ts","src/mcp/server.ts:236","AGENTS.md"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Downstream qualification should distinguish existing sink unit tests from request-lifetime integration tests and live native rendering. The linked tests establish token gating, increasing notification counters, labels and rejected-send isolation; they do not establish visible rendering or autonomous scheduling.","Include initial snapshots, timer drift, bounded waits, overlapping polls, retry-after handling and terminal timer teardown in downstream fallback validation.","No authored visual definitions or generated companions are attached. Prose supports this DEF-stage CLI assessment; no visual rendering or live client qualification is claimed."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"Reviewed the whole DEF, canonical artifact and all five completed substantive assessments against linked upstream requirements and current evidence. Story dependencies are acyclic and feasible. Shared attempt isolation, cancellation separation, concurrent-chat ownership and native/fallback delivery are coherent apart from gaps already reported. No additional distinct defect was demonstrated. Stakeholder-source verification remains incomplete.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-def.json",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-206db3426ffd4428.json",".insrc/artifacts/EPIC-206db3426ffd4428.json","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/DEF.md","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md","AGENTS.md","src/daemon/__tests__/workflow-progress-map.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/analyze-progress.test.ts","src/mcp/__tests__/progress-forward.test.ts","src/mcp/progress-forward.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress.ts","src/daemon/chat-sessions.ts — lifecycle and cleanup declarations","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts — status projection and detached-observer paths","vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts — saved turn and ownership seams","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-file-store.ts — capacity and active-chat seams"],"limitations":["The original stakeholder conversation referenced by citation c9 is unavailable in the supplied context and inspected records. As also recorded by the scope assessment, the exact requested retirement inventory and stakeholder authorization for superseding particular source stories cannot be independently verified. The DEF explicitly preserves traceability and requires approved successor linkage before retirement."],"advice":["Retain the existing findings contract-restart-recovery, vscode-conversation-closure, cli-background-lifetime and cli-fallback-cost-disclosure; this consistency assessment does not duplicate them.","The newer SPEC intentionally expands the July design's transient-only progress into recoverable observation and replaces its deprecated IDE-fork boundary with current VS Code delivery. Preserve compatible existing frames while documenting those supersessions in downstream designs.","Maintain a source-story crosswalk when retiring the July tracker entries. The current successor EPIC records tracker binding insors-ai/insrc#146.","No authored diagrams, UX definitions or generated companions are attached. DEF-stage prose adequately expresses the assessed ownership and behavior; no visual rendering verification is claimed. Downstream designs should make identity mappings, retention release, reconnect behavior and concurrent task presentation explicit."]}],"limitations":["The source conversation cited by /citations/8 is unavailable in the supplied context and inspected local records. Its citation states only 'consolidate all long-running progress stories into one epic.' Consequently, stakeholder intent concerning the exact retirement inventory, source-story preservation and approval/link-before-retirement ordering could not be independently verified. The DEF itself explicitly requires approved successor linkage before retirement.","The original stakeholder conversation referenced by citation c9 is unavailable in the supplied context and inspected records. As also recorded by the scope assessment, the exact requested retirement inventory and stakeholder authorization for superseding particular source stories cannot be independently verified. The DEF explicitly preserves traceability and requires approved successor linkage before retirement."],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"37a320486023b9464ba5c15a871a0f73ec59b4b6b0fc4827ae92bf08c92cdf0