n","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/0","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/1","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2","document:line:25","/body/constraints","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/7","/body/constraints/8","/body/stories","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/4","/citations/0","/citations/7","/citations/8","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-206db3426ffd4428.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-def.json","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/DEF.md","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md","AGENTS.md",".insrc/artifacts/EPIC-206db3426ffd4428.json",".insrc/artifacts/EPIC-6d6cfaf9a9b14bd4.json",".insrc/artifacts/STORY-6d6cfaf9a9b14bd4-s1.json",".insrc/artifacts/STORY-6d6cfaf9a9b14bd4-s2.json",".insrc/artifacts/STORY-6d6cfaf9a9b14bd4-s3.json","src/daemon/__tests__/workflow-progress-map.test.ts:16-66","src/daemon/__tests__/analyze-progress.test.ts:107-180","src/mcp/__tests__/progress-forward.test.ts:20-72","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress.ts"],"limitations":["The source conversation cited by /citations/8 is unavailable in the supplied context and inspected local records. Its citation states only 'consolidate all long-running progress stories into one epic.' Consequently, stakeholder intent concerning the exact retirement inventory, source-story preservation and approval/link-before-retirement ordering could not be independently verified. The DEF itself explicitly requires approved successor linkage before retirement."],"advice":["Before retiring tracker entries, record a concrete crosswalk from the July issue #41 and stories S001–S003 to the successor epic and stories, including completed capabilities retained and requirements superseded. The successor EPIC artifact already records tracker binding #146.","For this DEF scope assessment, prose adequately explains the required ownership and user-visible behavior. No authored visual definitions, generated companions or renderings are attached; no visual verification is claimed. Detailed interaction and UX artifacts can be assessed when the corresponding designs exist."]},{"chunkId":"contract","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector and its cited evidence. Producer assumptions are supported, and the shared contract covers measured progress, attempt isolation, authorization, bounded reconnects and cancellation separation. One upstream restart-recovery requirement lacks explicit acceptance coverage.","findings":[{"id":"contract-restart-recovery","severity":"MED","location":"docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:72","message":"The shared foundation specifies reconnect snapshots and unavailable-owner handling, but never requires recovery across a daemon restart. The cited SPEC explicitly requires durable snapshots/milestones, preserved terminal outcomes, and interrupted/unknown execution until the owner verifies survival or genuine resumption. Reconnecting to an unchanged daemon can satisfy the current acceptance criteria without exercising this boundary; marking missing progress stale also does not establish an honest execution state. Add a restart acceptance scenario covering retained state, owner revalidation and delayed prior-execution events, without restarting work.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:55","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:72","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:73","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md:33 — R10","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md — acceptance scenarios A8 and A13","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md — Non-functional targets: existing progress is transient and not persisted"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/assumptions","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/body/constraints/6","/body/stories/0","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/4","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/6","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-206db3426ffd4428.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-def.json","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md","src/daemon/__tests__/workflow-progress-map.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/analyze-progress.test.ts","src/mcp/__tests__/progress-forward.test.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress-persistence.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts:112","src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:475","src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts:703","src/mcp/progress-forward.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["When designing adapters, distinguish producer sequence counters from meaningful-progress revisions: existing review heartbeats and repeated analyze stage events advance their sequence/index without necessarily measuring new work.","No visual definitions or generated companions are attached to this DEF. Its shared-contract requirements can be assessed from prose; no visual rendering verification is claimed."]},{"chunkId":"producers","status":"passed","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the cited upstream requirements and current producer evidence. The producer stories preserve existing results, frames and cancellation; distinguish available workflow token batches from analysis stage-only progress; cover review retries, follow-up work and attempt authority; and address nested test results, reporter failure, abort and exit semantics. Their dependencies on the shared foundation are feasible. No demonstrated blocking defect was found within this assignment.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/2","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/3","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/body/constraints/6","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/6","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-206db3426ffd4428.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-def.json","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/DEF.md","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md — R2, R3, R8–R12, R17 and A2, A3, A8, A9, A16, A17","src/daemon/__tests__/workflow-progress-map.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/analyze-progress.test.ts","src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:466","src/daemon/analyze-rpc.ts:550","src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts — workflow.run and analyze.run.start registrations","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts:113","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/progress.test.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/progress.ts","src/workflow/review/design-review/coordinator.ts — attempt recovery, progress observation and publication boundaries","src/workflow/review/design-review/__tests__/coverage-progress.test.ts","src/daemon/tools/builtins/test/index.ts:212","src/daemon/tools/builtins/test/__tests__/test-runner-parity.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["In downstream designs, enumerate the supported workflow/analyze entry points and managed test reporters in an acceptance matrix. Include legacy terminal frames, observer absence, cancellation, unknown measurements, and explicit pass/fail/skip and elapsed-time assertions.","The assigned producer requirements are adequately assessable from prose at DEF stage. No visual definitions or generated companions are attached, and no visual rendering verification is claimed."]},{"chunkId":"vscode","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The assigned sections cover inline routing, attempt isolation, reconnects, runtime-owned retention and aggregate completion. Conversation closure/removal loses an explicit upstream lifecycle requirement.","findings":[{"id":"vscode-conversation-closure","severity":"MED","location":"docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md §6.5, acceptance criteria ac1–ac3","message":"The VS Code story defines chat switching, reconnecting and lost ownership, but does not define what happens to running tasks when their owning conversation is explicitly closed or removed. The cited SPEC R15 explicitly requires a detach/cancel disposition for this boundary. Neither stopping observation nor losing an owner determines that disposition. Add a requirement and acceptance scenario specifying whether execution continues, how retention associations are released, and where surviving results remain accessible; cancellation must retain the existing explicit-request and verified-termination semantics.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md §6.5 ac1–ac3","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md §5 k6–k7","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md — R15: explicit conversation closure/removal disposition","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md — R8: stopping observation versus cancellation","src/daemon/chat-sessions.ts — drop(), close() and dispose()"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/4","/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/constraints/3","/body/constraints/5","/body/constraints/6","/body/constraints/7","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/1","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/7","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-206db3426ffd4428.json","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md","AGENTS.md","vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-store.ts","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-file-store.ts — evictBeyondCap","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts — status projection, detached observation and terminal paths","vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts — lifecycle and lease seams","src/daemon/chat-sessions.ts",".insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-def.json — completed substantive feedback"],"limitations":[],"advice":["At downstream design, explicitly map extension conversation, daemon session, native session, invocation, task and attempt identities. Current protocol targeting and daemon pool identifiers are distinct.","Include Stop, setup failure, process death and detached-observer reconciliation in lifecycle validation. Current code contains separate status-writing paths that must share task-aware projection.","No UX definitions or generated companions are attached to this DEF; no visual rendering was verified. The prose supports DEF-stage assessment. Downstream UX artifacts should demonstrate concurrent task messages, terminal compaction and reconnect restoration."]},{"chunkId":"cli","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector and linked evidence. Token gating, original results, fixed fallback cadence, duplicate suppression and degraded recovery are covered. Native background lifetime qualification and user-visible fallback cost disclosure lose explicit upstream requirements.","findings":[{"id":"cli-background-lifetime","severity":"MED","location":"docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:151","message":"Native qualification lists connectivity, token forwarding, visible rendering and scheduling, but omits background/session lifetime as a separate capability. The cited SPEC requires this distinction and explicit reporting when vendor session activity cannot be maintained. Passing an in-request rendering test and a scheduling test does not establish observation after the launching turn ends or the native session exits. Add acceptance coverage for these boundaries per supported client/version/session, including honest limitation reporting and retained task/results for later reattachment without extending an expired progress token.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:150","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:151","docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:153","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md — R5, R7, R16; A4, A6, A15"]},{"id":"cli-fallback-cost-disclosure","severity":"LOW","location":"docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md:152","message":"The fallback is described internally as token-consuming and requires opt-in, but no requirement makes its token consumption and ordinary chat messages visible to the user. The upstream SPEC explicitly requires that disclosure. Preserve it in the opt-in acceptance scenario, including that unchanged polls can still consume tokens.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md — k5 and s6 ac3","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md — R6; A5, A10"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/5","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/constraints/3","/body/constraints/4","/body/constraints/6","/body/constraints/7","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2","/citations/2","/citations/5","/citations/7","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-206db3426ffd4428.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-def.json — completed substantive feedback","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md","src/mcp/__tests__/progress-forward.test.ts","src/mcp/progress-forward.ts","src/mcp/server.ts:236","AGENTS.md"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Downstream qualification should distinguish existing sink unit tests from request-lifetime integration tests and live native rendering. The linked tests establish token gating, increasing notification counters, labels and rejected-send isolation; they do not establish visible rendering or autonomous scheduling.","Include initial snapshots, timer drift, bounded waits, overlapping polls, retry-after handling and terminal timer teardown in downstream fallback validation.","No authored visual definitions or generated companions are attached. Prose supports this DEF-stage CLI assessment; no visual rendering or live client qualification is claimed."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"Reviewed the whole DEF, canonical artifact and all five completed substantive assessments against linked upstream requirements and current evidence. Story dependencies are acyclic and feasible. Shared attempt isolation, cancellation separation, concurrent-chat ownership and native/fallback delivery are coherent apart from gaps already reported. No additional distinct defect was demonstrated. Stakeholder-source verification remains incomplete.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/epics/show-long-running-task-progress-chat-E20261109206db342/DEF.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/consolidated-chat-progress-def.json",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-206db3426ffd4428.json",".insrc/artifacts/EPIC-206db3426ffd4428.json","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/DEF.md","docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md","docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md","AGENTS.md","src/daemon/__tests__/workflow-progress-map.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/analyze-progress.test.ts","src/mcp/__tests__/progress-forward.test.ts","src/mcp/progress-forward.ts","src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress.ts","src/daemon/chat-sessions.ts — lifecycle and cleanup declarations","vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts — status projection and detached-observer paths","vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts — saved turn and ownership seams","vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-file-store.ts — capacity and active-chat seams"],"limitations":["The original stakeholder conversation referenced by citation c9 is unavailable in the supplied context and inspected records. As also recorded by the scope assessment, the exact requested retirement inventory and stakeholder authorization for superseding particular source stories cannot be independently verified. The DEF explicitly preserves traceability and requires approved successor linkage before retirement."],"advice":["Retain the existing findings contract-restart-recovery, vscode-conversation-closure, cli-background-lifetime and cli-fallback-cost-disclosure; this consistency assessment does not duplicate them.","The newer SPEC intentionally expands the July design's transient-only progress into recoverable observation and replaces its deprecated IDE-fork boundary with current VS Code delivery. Preserve compatible existing frames while documenting those supersessions in downstream designs.","Maintain a source-story crosswalk when retiring the July tracker entries. The current successor EPIC records tracker binding insors-ai/insrc#146.","No authored diagrams, UX definitions or generated companions are attached. DEF-stage prose adequately expresses the assessed ownership and behavior; no visual rendering verification is claimed. Downstream designs should make identity mappings, retention release, reconnect behavior and concurrent task presentation explicit."]}],"limitations":["The source conversation cited by /citations/8 is unavailable in the supplied context and inspected local records. Its citation states only 'consolidate all long-running progress stories into one epic.' Consequently, stakeholder intent concerning the exact retirement inventory, source-story preservation and approval/link-before-retirement ordering could not be independently verified. The DEF itself explicitly requires approved successor linkage before retirement.","The original stakeholder conversation referenced by citation c9 is unavailable in the supplied context and inspected records. As also recorded by the scope assessment, the exact requested retirement inventory and stakeholder authorization for superseding particular source stories cannot be independently verified. The DEF explicitly preserves traceability and requires approved successor linkage before retirement."],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"37a320486023b9464ba5c15a871a0f73ec59b4b6b0fc4827ae92bf08c92cdf07"},"finishedAt":"2026-11-09T06:11:53.443Z"},{"number":2,"status":"incomplete","preparationKind":"impact","baseline":{"subjectFingerprints":{"canonical":"ff29240baa1ead3d4147c6cb7eae7f86d330a6949fcad3152c91ab70675415cc","document":"c88aa2d24b97f96aa003a53b281e603d57a2cec48fb806aa9148903bbc55b25e"},"contentIdentity":"26c1e5ffb7ee1fa1c25df6ff0f56b6ff149de288677c66baed73983ebd390cb8","reviewedContent":{"canonical":"{\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"workflow\": \"define\",\n    \"runId\": \"wf-1794203852552-tg40ov\",\n    \"repoPath\": \"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-09T06:00:04.355Z\",\n    \"epicCreatedAt\": \"2026-11-09T06:00:04.355Z\",\n    \"attribution\": {\n      \"outputs\": [\n        {\n          \"role\": \"(client)\",\n          \"tier\": \"core\",\n          \"runner\": \"cli-codex\",\n          \"model\": \"unknown\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"elapsedMs\": 151801,\n    \"repoIndexedAt\": null,\n    \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n    \"epicHash\": \"206db3426ffd4428\",\n    \"epicSlug\": \"show-long-running-task-progress-chat\",\n    \"authoredBy\": \"controller\",\n    \"revision\": 2,\n    \"envelope\": {\n      \"description\": \"\",\n      \"references\": [],\n      \"attachments\": []\n    },\n    \"lifecycle\": {\n      \"status\": \"draft\",\n      \"revision\": {\n        \"number\": 2,\n        \"contentHash\": \"8ebe74dc406131f655417862a731249d2bcf2bcda51dfc81c0448a9e864a5a22\",\n        \"at\": \"2026-11-09T06:14:06.455Z\",\n        \"by\": {\n          \"id\": \"insrc:system\",\n          \"kind\": \"system\",\n          \"properties\": {}\n        }\n      },\n      \"signoffs\": [],\n      \"review\": {\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"reviewer\": {\n          \"id\": \"agent:design-review-daemon\",\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"party\": \"daemon\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"party\": \"daemon\",\n        \"verdict\": \"block\",\n        \"counts\": {\n          \"HIGH\": 0,\n          \"MED\": 3,\n          \"LOW\": 1\n        },\n        \"at\": \"2026-11-09T06:11:53.443Z\",\n        \"report\": {\n          \"entityId\": \"DEF-206db3426ffd4428\",\n          \"type\": \"change-log-entry\",\n          \"relation\": \"reviews\",\n          \"fragment\": \"2064ae51c18135d5c3a29d3159774e8706c5427431c56e20dbd41bd67d9732d6\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"body\": {\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"audience\": \"product\",\n      \"prose\": \"Follow long-running reviews, test sweeps, workflow operations and analysis from the conversation that launched them. See measured progress and the final result while work continues across turns, chat switches and supported reconnects. Native delivery needs no extra model calls, with optional one-minute polling where direct delivery is unavailable.\"\n    },\n    \"problem\": \"Users following long-running daemon workflows, analysis, reviews and test sweeps receive uneven progress feedback across clients and often have to ask whether work is still running. Output silence makes it hard to distinguish measured work, a healthy wait and a lost observer. A chat can appear finished or age out while its background task is still running, and switching conversations or reconnecting can hide the task's latest state.\",\n    \"nonGoals\": [\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Changes to review execution, workflow stages, approval gates or model providers\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Observation follows existing execution ownership and results.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"insrc TUI changes, deprecated insrc-ide work, or third-party CLI patches\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Initial delivery targets VS Code chat and verified native CLI surfaces.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"General job scheduling, arbitrary process attachment or automatic task restart\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Initial delegates observe instrumented, authorized executions.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Fabricated ETA or progress, raw model output as progress, and universal MCP Tasks support\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Progress is measured, bounded and capability-specific.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"assumptions\": [\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Current workflow and analyze producers already expose some shared progress. Workflow token batches and analyze stage frames have distinct evidence and availability.\",\n        \"confidence\": \"high\",\n        \"source\": \"c4\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Analyze producer tests cover stage frames and explicitly show cases where no token delta is emitted.\",\n        \"confidence\": \"high\",\n        \"source\": \"c5\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"MCP forwarding code and tests exist. Native rendering and autonomous scheduling require separate live qualification.\",\n        \"confidence\": \"high\",\n        \"source\": \"c6\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Committed code-review checkpoints expose phase, active task and completed tasks as measured inputs.\",\n        \"confidence\": \"high\",\n        \"source\": \"c7\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"constraints\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k1\",\n        \"type\": \"contract\",\n        \"text\": \"Cover workflow and analyze operations through their supported IPC entry points, design reviews, code reviews and managed test sweeps with a shared authorized task/attempt progress contract.\",\n        \"source\": \"c1\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k2\",\n        \"type\": \"invariant\",\n        \"text\": \"Reuse the existing Unix IPC and typed progress/delta seams compatibly. Preserve existing frame semantics, cancellation, final results and behavior for clients without progress observers. Client database access remains IPC-only.\",\n        \"source\": \"c2\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k3\",\n        \"type\": \"contract\",\n        \"text\": \"Each initial task delegate supplies bounded structured progress() for an authorized attempt, shared by direct delivery and optional polling. Measured phase, counts, active unit, milestones and freshness stay distinct from lifecycle, connectivity, liveness and retention. Unknown measurements stay unknown.\",\n        \"source\": \"c3\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k4\",\n        \"type\": \"contract\",\n        \"text\": \"Publish native progress with zero extra model invocations. MCP forwards monotonic progress with an optional caller token only during its valid request lifetime. No token means normal completion without notifications. Live-qualify visible rendering independently of protocol support. Qualify delivery beyond the launching turn and across native session exit separately from in-request rendering and scheduling. Retain results for authorized reattachment where native session activity cannot be maintained.\",\n        \"source\": \"c3\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k5\",\n        \"type\": \"stakeholder\",\n        \"text\": \"Optional token-consuming agent fallback uses one shared fixed 60-second healthy schedule per task. Suppress duplicate narration without slowing cadence. Report degraded or unavailable scheduling and stop observation at terminal state. Before opt-in, disclose that fallback can consume agent tokens even on unchanged polls and can produce ordinary chat messages.\",\n        \"source\": \"c3\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k6\",\n        \"type\": \"contract\",\n        \"text\": \"Route one typed inline message to the owning VS Code chat and update it across turns and chat switching. Runtime task ownership renews bounded activity independently of observers and respects waiting-input, multiple attempts and unrelated chat concurrency. Explicit conversation closure detaches presentation. Removing the conversation releases its retention association and preserves authorized access to surviving task state and results through the owning project. Running execution continues unless the user explicitly cancels it.\",\n        \"source\": \"c3\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k7\",\n        \"type\": \"invariant\",\n        \"text\": \"Restore bounded authorized snapshots and milestones with cursor or explicit resync on reconnect. Preserve verified terminal outcomes, prevent stale attempts from overwriting newer state, and reconcile lost owners honestly. Stopping observation and cancelling execution are separate actions. Persist bounded snapshots, milestones and verified terminal outcomes across daemon restarts. Mark nonterminal execution interrupted or unknown until its owner verifies survival or genuine resumption. Discard delayed events from prior execution epochs.\",\n        \"source\": \"c3\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k8\",\n        \"type\": \"convention\",\n        \"text\": \"Use current VS Code and daemon entry points and qualify native Claude Code, Codex and Vibe per client. No deprecated client gates, TUI changes or direct provider API access.\",\n        \"source\": \"c8\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k9\",\n        \"type\": \"convention\",\n        \"text\": \"Preserve traceability to July epic #41 and its three stories #42–#44. Treat them as source requirements for this successor. Tracker retirement is a separate decision after successor approval and linkage.\",\n        \"source\": \"c9\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"title\": \"Show long-running task progress in chat\",\n    \"flavor\": \"enhancement\",\n    \"stories\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"s1\",\n        \"title\": \"Track long-running work consistently across executors\",\n        \"userValue\": \"Users receive trustworthy, current progress for an authorized execution attempt even when the operation is quiet.\",\n        \"sizeEstimate\": \"L\",\n        \"existingCapabilityRefs\": [\n          \"c2\",\n          \"c4\",\n          \"c5\",\n          \"c7\"\n        ],\n        \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac1\",\n            \"given\": \"Two authorized attempts are running\",\n            \"when\": \"their measurements advance, arrive out of order or repeat\",\n            \"then\": \"each exposes its own meaningful revision, measured phase and counts with declared units, source freshness and milestones. Duplicates, sample times and heartbeats do not fabricate progress.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\",\n              \"k3\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac2\",\n            \"given\": \"An observer reconnects or falls behind\",\n            \"when\": \"it requests the latest authorized state\",\n            \"then\": \"it receives the latest bounded snapshot and relevant milestones, then resumes or explicitly resyncs. Terminal results remain stable and stale attempts cannot overwrite new ones.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac3\",\n            \"given\": \"An owner becomes unavailable or a user stops observation\",\n            \"when\": \"the observation is reconciled\",\n            \"then\": \"missing progress is stale or unknown, and no execution is restarted or marked complete from loss of observation. Explicit cancellation stays pending until termination is verified.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac4\",\n            \"given\": \"An unrelated user or chat requests task details or logs\",\n            \"when\": \"access is evaluated\",\n            \"then\": \"unauthorized access is rejected and approved observations stay bounded and redacted without exposing raw model text, credentials or unbounded logs.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k2\",\n              \"k3\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac5\",\n            \"given\": \"A reader compares the successor with July epic #41 and stories #42–#44\",\n            \"when\": \"they trace the predecessor scope\",\n            \"then\": \"the successor links the source epic and identifies all three story records, preserving the original requirements and their history.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k9\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac6\",\n            \"given\": \"Running and terminal attempts have persisted snapshots and the daemon restarts\",\n            \"when\": \"an authorized observer reattaches and delayed events from the previous execution epoch arrive\",\n            \"then\": \"the last verified milestones and terminal results remain available. A nonterminal attempt is interrupted or unknown until its owner verifies survival or genuine resumption. Delayed events cannot replace newer state, and reattachment starts no execution.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"s2\",\n        \"title\": \"Preserve live progress for workflows and analysis\",\n        \"userValue\": \"Users can distinguish a quiet workflow or analysis from active stage advancement without losing current client compatibility.\",\n        \"sizeEstimate\": \"M\",\n        \"dependsOn\": [\n          \"s1\"\n        ],\n        \"existingCapabilityRefs\": [\n          \"c1\",\n          \"c2\",\n          \"c4\",\n          \"c5\"\n        ],\n        \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac1\",\n            \"given\": \"A supported daemon workflow and analysis run end to end\",\n            \"when\": \"each enters a new stage and reports supported measurements\",\n            \"then\": \"both expose the same progress contract with the current stage and measured ongoing production, including batched token counts only where actually available. Missing counts remain unknown.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\",\n              \"k2\",\n              \"k3\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac2\",\n            \"given\": \"A legacy client or a caller without a progress observer starts either operation\",\n            \"when\": \"it runs to a terminal outcome\",\n            \"then\": \"existing stream semantics, operation results and cancellation behavior are preserved. Progress ends once the terminal outcome is delivered.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\",\n              \"k2\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"s3\",\n        \"title\": \"Report design and code review milestones\",\n        \"userValue\": \"Review participants see which stage or task is active and which measured work has finished.\",\n        \"sizeEstimate\": \"M\",\n        \"dependsOn\": [\n          \"s1\"\n        ],\n        \"existingCapabilityRefs\": [\n          \"c3\",\n          \"c7\"\n        ],\n        \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac1\",\n            \"given\": \"A design review and a committed task code review are running\",\n            \"when\": \"phases, tasks, checks or supported chunks advance\",\n            \"then\": \"the review-specific measurements show active and completed units, retries and discovered follow-up work separately. A quiet worker can report health without incrementing counts.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\",\n              \"k3\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac2\",\n            \"given\": \"A review is interrupted or resumed\",\n            \"when\": \"an observer returns or a delayed event arrives\",\n            \"then\": \"the latest verified attempt remains authoritative and findings, publication and approval gates retain their existing behavior.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"s4\",\n        \"title\": \"Report managed test-sweep counts and final outcome\",\n        \"userValue\": \"Users see test activity, reliable pass/fail/skip counts and the verified result before reading the full log.\",\n        \"sizeEstimate\": \"M\",\n        \"dependsOn\": [\n          \"s1\"\n        ],\n        \"existingCapabilityRefs\": [\n          \"c3\"\n        ],\n        \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac1\",\n            \"given\": \"A managed test command discovers and runs suites\",\n            \"when\": \"its reporter emits nested results, retries or partial failures\",\n            \"then\": \"the active suite and measured discovery/execution/completion counts are exposed with declared units and no double counting. Detailed output stays separately accessible.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\",\n              \"k3\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac2\",\n            \"given\": \"The command is aborted, exits nonzero or its reporter fails\",\n            \"when\": \"a terminal update is rendered\",\n            \"then\": \"incomplete or unsuccessful work is represented truthfully and the original command and exit semantics are preserved.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k2\",\n              \"k3\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"s5\",\n        \"title\": \"Keep inline progress with its originating VS Code chat\",\n        \"userValue\": \"Users can switch chats and continue working while background tasks stay visible and retain their own session.\",\n        \"sizeEstimate\": \"L\",\n        \"dependsOn\": [\n          \"s1\",\n          \"s2\",\n          \"s3\",\n          \"s4\"\n        ],\n        \"existingCapabilityRefs\": [\n          \"c2\",\n          \"c3\"\n        ],\n        \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac1\",\n            \"given\": \"A review, test sweep, workflow or analysis is launched in chat A\",\n            \"when\": \"the user starts another turn, switches chats or reconnects\",\n            \"then\": \"a typed client surface updates one existing message in A without extra model calls and retains one compact terminal result. No event crosses into chat B.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k2\",\n              \"k4\",\n              \"k6\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac2\",\n            \"given\": \"Chat A has verified live work and no attached observers\",\n            \"when\": \"its idle window elapses or session capacity is reached\",\n            \"then\": \"the execution owner keeps A retained without agent polling or visible ticks. B can run independently and observation never owns an execution lock.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k6\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac3\",\n            \"given\": \"Chat A has two tasks, a newer turn and an unresolved decision\",\n            \"when\": \"an old attempt ends or a heartbeat arrives\",\n            \"then\": \"waiting-input takes precedence and done is projected only after all obligations end. Lost ownership expires within a bound and late events cannot resurrect work.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k6\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac4\",\n            \"given\": \"An owning conversation has a running task\",\n            \"when\": \"the user explicitly closes or removes the conversation\",\n            \"then\": \"presentation detaches and execution continues. Removing the conversation releases its retention association and preserves authorized access to surviving task state and results from the project. If the user explicitly cancels, cancellation remains pending until the executor verifies termination.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k6\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"s6\",\n        \"title\": \"Deliver progress in supported native CLI chats\",\n        \"userValue\": \"Claude Code, Codex and Vibe users get progress through capabilities verified for their own client.\",\n        \"sizeEstimate\": \"L\",\n        \"dependsOn\": [\n          \"s1\",\n          \"s2\",\n          \"s3\",\n          \"s4\"\n        ],\n        \"existingCapabilityRefs\": [\n          \"c3\",\n          \"c6\"\n        ],\n        \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac1\",\n            \"given\": \"A long-running MCP request includes a valid caller progress token\",\n            \"when\": \"the operation reports progress and then finishes\",\n            \"then\": \"notifications use that token only during its valid lifetime, expose monotonic measured progress, and finish with the original result. A no-token request completes normally without notifications.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k2\",\n              \"k4\",\n              \"k8\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac2\",\n            \"given\": \"A client claims native progress or background scheduling support\",\n            \"when\": \"it is qualified end to end\",\n            \"then\": \"tool connectivity, token forwarding, visible rendering, scheduled observation, background lifetime after the launching turn and behavior on native session exit are verified separately for that client/version/session. Verified native delivery consumes no extra model calls.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k4\",\n              \"k8\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac3\",\n            \"given\": \"A user explicitly opts into fallback on a healthy host after being told that even unchanged polls can consume agent tokens and updates can produce ordinary chat messages\",\n            \"when\": \"several observers attach and the task alternates changes with unchanged snapshots\",\n            \"then\": \"one schedule returns current details every 60 seconds, suppressing duplicate narration without delaying the next poll. Terminal and action-required changes appear by the next healthy poll.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\",\n              \"k5\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac4\",\n            \"given\": \"A fallback host loses scheduling or connectivity\",\n            \"when\": \"observation cannot continue on schedule\",\n            \"then\": \"the client reports a degraded or suspended observer, resumes the fixed healthy cadence after recovery where supported, and never implies execution cancellation.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k5\",\n              \"k7\",\n              \"k8\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac5\",\n            \"given\": \"A native client can render progress during a request but cannot maintain native observation after the launching turn or session exit\",\n            \"when\": \"the request or session ends while execution remains owned\",\n            \"then\": \"the client surfaces the capability limit. Expired progress tokens are never reused, execution is not cancelled, and authorized reattachment can recover the saved task state and result.\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k4\",\n              \"k7\",\n              \"k8\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"openQuestions\": [],\n    \"functionalDefinition\": {\n      \"requirements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261109206db342:FR001\",\n          \"statement\": \"Users see the latest verified stage, measurable work and terminal outcome for supported long-running operations.\",\n          \"scope\": \"doc\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261109206db342:FR002\",\n          \"statement\": \"Users can follow several tasks in their own chats across turns, switches and reconnects, with observations scoped to the right attempt.\",\n          \"scope\": \"doc\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261109206db342:FR003\",\n          \"statement\": \"Supported clients show native updates without extra model calls, and users can explicitly enable one-minute fallback observation where supported.\",\n          \"scope\": \"doc\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"kind\": \"prior-artifact\",\n      \"ref\": \"docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/DEF.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"kind\": \"prior-artifact\",\n      \"ref\": \"docs/epics/stream-incremental-progress-from-daemon-calling-E202607196d6cfaf9/HLD.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"kind\": \"prior-artifact\",\n      \"ref\": \"docs/standalone/show-background-task-progress-chat-E2026110407024f1d/SPEC.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/daemon/__tests__/workflow-progress-map.test.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c5\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/daemon/__tests__/analyze-progress.test.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/mcp/__tests__/progress-forward.test.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8\",\n      \"kind\": \"convention\",\n      \"ref\": \"AGENTS.md\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c9\",\n      \"kind\": \"prior-artifact\",\n      \"ref\": \"https://github.com/insors-ai/insrc/issues/41\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","document":"<!-- insrc:artifact DEF-206db3426ffd4428 -->\n\n# Epic: show-long-running-task-progress-chat\n\n## Summary\n\n**Flavor:** enhancement\n**Tracker:** [insors-ai/insrc#146](https://github.com/insors-ai/insrc/issues/146)\n\nFollow long-running reviews, test sweeps, workflow operations and analysis from the conversation that launched them. See measured progress and the final result while work continues across turns, chat switches and supported reconnects. Native delivery needs no extra model calls, with optional one-minute polling where direct delivery is unavailable.\n\n## Contents\n\n1. [Problem](#1-problem)\n2. [Functional requirements](#2-functional-requirements)\n3. [Non-goals](#3-non-goals)\n4. [Assumptions](#4-assumptions)\n5. [Constraints](#5-constraints)\n6. [Stories](#6-stories)\n7. [References](#7-references)\n\n## 1. Problem\n\nUsers following long-running daemon workflows, analysis, reviews and test sweeps receive uneven progress feedback across clients and often have to ask whether work is still running. Output silence makes it hard to distinguish measured work, a healthy wait and a lost observer. A chat can appear finished or age out while its background task is still running, and switching conversations or reconnecting can hide the task's latest state.\n\n## 2. Functional requirements\n\n- **E20261109206db342:FR001** — Users see the latest verified stage, measurable work and terminal outcome for supported long-running operations.\n- **E20261109206db342:FR002** — Users can follow several tasks in their own chats across turns, switches and reconnects, with observations scoped to the right attempt.\n- **E20261109206db342:FR003** — Supported clients show native updates without extra model calls, and users can explicitly enable one-minute fallback observation where supported.\n\n## 3. Non-goals\n\n- **Changes to review execution, workflow stages, approval gates or model providers** — Observation follows existing execution ownership and results.\n- **insrc TUI changes, deprecated insrc-ide work, or third-party CLI patches** — Initial delivery targets VS Code chat and verified native CLI surfaces.\n- **General job scheduling, arbitrary process attachment or automatic task restart** — Initial delegates observe instrumented, authorized executions.\n- **Fabricated ETA or progress, raw model output as progress, and universal MCP Tasks support** — Progress is measured, bounded and capability-specific.\n\n## 4. Assumptions\n\n- `high` Current workflow and analyze producers already expose some shared progress. Workflow token batches and analyze stage frames have distinct evidence and availability. [[c4]]\n- `high` Analyze producer tests cover stage frames and explicitly show cases where no token delta is emitted. [[c5]]\n- `high` MCP forwarding code and tests exist. Native rendering and autonomous scheduling require separate live qualification. [[c6]]\n- `high` Committed code-review checkpoints expose phase, active task and completed tasks as measured inputs. [[c7]]\n\n## 5. Constraints\n\n| ID | Type | Text | Source |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `k1` | contract | Cover workflow and analyze operations through their supported IPC entry points, design reviews, code reviews and managed test sweeps with a shared authorized task/attempt progress contract. | [[c1]] |\n| `k2` | invariant | Reuse the existing Unix IPC and typed progress/delta seams compatibly. Preserve existing frame semantics, cancellation, final results and behavior for clients without progress observers. Client database access remains IPC-only. | [[c2]] |\n| `k3` | contract | Each initial task delegate supplies bounded structured progress() for an authorized attempt, shared by direct delivery and optional polling. Measured phase, counts, active unit, milestones and freshness stay distinct from lifecycle, connectivity, liveness and retention. Unknown measurements stay unknown. | [[c3]] |\n| `k4` | contract | Publish native progress with zero extra model invocations. MCP forwards monotonic progress with an optional caller token only during its valid request lifetime. No token means normal completion without notifications. Live-qualify visible rendering independently of protocol support. Qualify delivery beyond the launching turn and across native session exit separately from in-request rendering and scheduling. Retain results for authorized reattachment where native session activity cannot be maintained. | [[c3]] |\n| `k5` | stakeholder | Optional token-consuming agent fallback uses one shared fixed 60-second healthy schedule per task. Suppress duplicate narration without slowing cadence. Report degraded or unavailable scheduling and stop observation at terminal state. Before opt-in, disclose that fallback can consume agent tokens even on unchanged polls and can produce ordinary chat messages. | [[c3]] |\n| `k6` | contract | Route one typed inline message to the owning VS Code chat and update it across turns and chat switching. Runtime task ownership renews bounded activity independently of observers and respects waiting-input, multiple attempts and unrelated chat concurrency. Explicit conversation closure detaches presentation. Removing the conversation releases its retention association and preserves authorized access to surviving task state and results through the owning project. Running execution continues unless the user explicitly cancels it. | [[c3]] |\n| `k7` | invariant | Restore bounded authorized snapshots and milestones with cursor or explicit resync on reconnect. Preserve verified terminal outcomes, prevent stale attempts from overwriting newer state, and reconcile lost owners honestly. Stopping observation and cancelling execution are separate actions. Persist bounded snapshots, milestones and verified terminal outcomes across daemon restarts. Mark nonterminal execution interrupted or unknown until its owner verifies survival or genuine resumption. Discard delayed events from prior execution epochs. | [[c3]] |\n| `k8` | convention | Use current VS Code and daemon entry points and qualify native Claude Code, Codex and Vibe per client. No deprecated client gates, TUI changes or direct provider API access. | [[c8]] |\n| `k9` | convention | Preserve traceability to July epic #41 and its three stories #42–#44. Treat them as source requirements for this successor. Tracker retirement is a separate decision after successor approval and linkage. | [[c9]] |\n\n## 6. Stories\n\n### 6.1 STORY-206db3426ffd4428-s1 — Track long-running work consistently across executors\n\n**User value:** `size: L`\n\nUsers receive trustworthy, current progress for an authorized execution attempt even when the operation is quiet.\n\n**Extends:** [[c2]] [[c4]] [[c5]] [[c7]]\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n\n- **ac1:** Given Two authorized attempts are running, when their measurements advance, arrive out of order or repeat, then each exposes its own meaningful revision, measured phase and counts with declared units, source freshness and milestones. Duplicates, sample times and heartbeats do not fabricate progress.. _(operationalizes `k1`, `k3`, `k7`)_\n- **ac2:** Given An observer reconnects or falls behind, when it requests the latest authorized state, then it receives the latest bounded snapshot and relevant milestones, then resumes or explicitly resyncs. Terminal results remain stable and stale attempts cannot overwrite new ones.. _(operationalizes `k3`, `k7`)_\n- **ac3:** Given An owner becomes unavailable or a user stops observation, when the observation is reconciled, then missing progress is stale or unknown, and no execution is restarted or marked complete from loss of observation. Explicit cancellation stays pending until termination is verified.. _(operationalizes `k7`)_\n- **ac4:** Given An unrelated user or chat requests task details or logs, when access is evaluated, then unauthorized access is rejected and approved observations stay bounded and redacted without exposing raw model text, credentials or unbounded logs.. _(operationalizes `k2`, `k3`, `k7`)_\n- **ac5:** Given A reader compares the successor with July epic #41 and stories #42–#44, when they trace the predecessor scope, then the successor links the source epic and identifies all three story records, preserving the original requirements and their history.. _(operationalizes `k9`)_\n- **ac6:** Given Running and terminal attempts have persisted snapshots and the daemon restarts, when an authorized observer reattaches and delayed events from the previous execution epoch arrive, then the last verified milestones and terminal results remain available. A nonterminal attempt is interrupted or unknown until its owner verifies survival or genuine resumption. Delayed events cannot replace newer state, and reattachment starts no execution.. _(operationalizes `k3`, `k7`)_\n\n### 6.2 STORY-206db3426ffd4428-s2 — Preserve live progress for workflows and analysis\n\n**User value:** `size: M`\n\nUsers can distinguish a quiet workflow or analysis from active stage advancement without losing current client compatibility.\n\n**Depends on:** `s1`\n\n**Extends:** [[c1]] [[c2]] [[c4]] [[c5]]\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n\n- **ac1:** Given A supported daemon workflow and analysis run end to end, when each enters a new stage and reports supported measurements, then both expose the same progress contract with the current stage and measured ongoing production, including batched token counts only where actually available. Missing counts remain unknown.. _(operationalizes `k1`, `k2`, `k3`)_\n- **ac2:** Given A legacy client or a caller without a progress observer starts either operation, when it runs to a terminal outcome, then existing stream semantics, operation results and cancellation behavior are preserved. Progress ends once the terminal outcome is delivered.. _(operationalizes `k1`, `k2`, `k7`)_\n\n### 6.3 STORY-206db3426ffd4428-s3 — Report design and code review milestones\n\n**User value:** `size: M`\n\nReview participants see which stage or task is active and which measured work has finished.\n\n**Depends on:** `s1`\n\n**Extends:** [[c3]] [[c7]]\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n\n- **ac1:** Given A design review and a committed task code review are running, when phases, tasks, checks or supported chunks advance, then the review-specific measurements show active and completed units, retries and discovered follow-up work separately. A quiet worker can report health without incrementing counts.. _(operationalizes `k1`, `k3`)_\n- **ac2:** Given A review is interrupted or resumed, when an observer returns or a delayed event arrives, then the latest verified attempt remains authoritative and findings, publication and approval gates retain their existing behavior.. _(operationalizes `k3`, `k7`)_\n\n### 6.4 STORY-206db3426ffd4428-s4 — Report managed test-sweep counts and final outcome\n\n**User value:** `size: M`\n\nUsers see test activity, reliable pass/fail/skip counts and the verified result before reading the full log.\n\n**Depends on:** `s1`\n\n**Extends:** [[c3]]\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n\n- **ac1:** Given A managed test command discovers and runs suites, when its reporter emits nested results, retries or partial failures, then the active suite and measured discovery/execution/completion counts are exposed with declared units and no double counting. Detailed output stays separately accessible.. _(operationalizes `k1`, `k3`)_\n- **ac2:** Given The command is aborted, exits nonzero or its reporter fails, when a terminal update is rendered, then incomplete or unsuccessful work is represented truthfully and the original command and exit semantics are preserved.. _(operationalizes `k2`, `k3`, `k7`)_\n\n### 6.5 STORY-206db3426ffd4428-s5 — Keep inline progress with its originating VS Code chat\n\n**User value:** `size: L`\n\nUsers can switch chats and continue working while background tasks stay visible and retain their own session.\n\n**Depends on:** `s1`, `s2`, `s3`, `s4`\n\n**Extends:** [[c2]] [[c3]]\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n\n- **ac1:** Given A review, test sweep, workflow or analysis is launched in chat A, when the user starts another turn, switches chats or reconnects, then a typed client surface updates one existing message in A without extra model calls and retains one compact terminal result. No event crosses into chat B.. _(operationalizes `k2`, `k4`, `k6`, `k7`)_\n- **ac2:** Given Chat A has verified live work and no attached observers, when its idle window elapses or session capacity is reached, then the execution owner keeps A retained without agent polling or visible ticks. B can run independently and observation never owns an execution lock.. _(operationalizes `k6`, `k7`)_\n- **ac3:** Given Chat A has two tasks, a newer turn and an unresolved decision, when an old attempt ends or a heartbeat arrives, then waiting-input takes precedence and done is projected only after all obligations end. Lost ownership expires within a bound and late events cannot resurrect work.. _(operationalizes `k6`, `k7`)_\n- **ac4:** Given An owning conversation has a running task, when the user explicitly closes or removes the conversation, then presentation detaches and execution continues. Removing the conversation releases its retention association and preserves authorized access to surviving task state and results from the project. If the user explicitly cancels, cancellation remains pending until the executor verifies termination.. _(operationalizes `k6`, `k7`)_\n\n### 6.6 STORY-206db3426ffd4428-s6 — Deliver progress in supported native CLI chats\n\n**User value:** `size: L`\n\nClaude Code, Codex and Vibe users get progress through capabilities verified for their own client.\n\n**Depends on:** `s1`, `s2`, `s3`, `s4`\n\n**Extends:** [[c3]] [[c6]]\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n\n- **ac1:** Given A long-running MCP request includes a valid caller progress token, when the operation reports progress and then finishes, then notifications use that token only during its valid lifetime, expose monotonic measured progress, and finish with the original result. A no-token request completes normally without notifications.. _(operationalizes `k2`, `k4`, `k8`)_\n- **ac2:** Given A client claims native progress or background scheduling support, when it is qualified end to end, then tool connectivity, token forwarding, visible rendering, scheduled observation, background lifetime after the launching turn and behavior on native session exit are verified separately for that client/version/session. Verified native delivery consumes no extra model calls.. _(operationalizes `k4`, `k8`)_\n- **ac3:** Given A user explicitly opts into fallback on a healthy host after being told that even unchanged polls can consume agent tokens and updates can produce ordinary chat messages, when several observers attach and the task alternates changes with unchanged snapshots, then one schedule returns current details every 60 seconds, suppressing duplicate narration without delaying the next poll. Terminal and action-required changes appear by the next healthy poll.. _(operationalizes `k3`, `k5`)_\n- **ac4:** Given A fallback host loses scheduling or connectivity, when observation cannot continue on schedule, then the client reports a degraded or suspended observer, resumes the fixed healthy cadence after recovery where supported, and never implies execution cancellation.. _(operationalizes `k5`, `k7`, `k8`)_\n- **ac5:** Given A native client can render progress during a request but cannot maintain native observation after the launching turn or session exit, when the request or session ends while execution remains owned, then the client surfaces the capability limit. Expired progress tokens are never reused, execution is not cancelled, and authorized reattachment can recover the saved task state and result.. _(operationalizes `k4`, `k7`, `k8`)_\n\n## 7